Package: marineSim
Title: Spatiotemporal Random Forests for Marine Species Distribution Modelling Under Data Limitation
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Ebenezer", "Afrifa-Yamoah", email = "e.afrifayamoah@ecu.edu.au",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Francky", "Fouedjio", role = "aut"),
    person("Ute", "Mueller", role = "aut"),
    person("Kathryn", "McMahon", role = "aut"),
    person("Glenn A.", "Hyndes", role = "aut"))
Description: Tools for the simulation benchmark and applied analysis behind the
    spatiotemporal random forest (stRF) method for marine species distribution
    modelling. The package provides a Matern Gaussian random field generator, a
    configurable ground truth world simulator with spatial and temporal structure,
    the stRF feature engineering layer (multi scale spatial lags, temporal lags and
    Euclidean distance fields), thin wrappers around competing models (GLM, GAM,
    spatial random forest and a geostatistical comparator), a predictive gain
    decomposition, and an area of applicability routine for honest extrapolation
    assessment. The design is built for the data limited regime of tens of survey
    sites observed over a handful of time points.
